31,"Went through fire passage","Set by crawling through the room7 fireplace passage to room11."
32,"Acid neutralized","Set by pouring the baking soda on the spilled acid at the lab table. With the Complete formula (36) in inventory, game code then turns flag 33 ON."
33,"Ready to mix the drug","Set by game code (re-derived every main-loop pass) once the acid is neutralized (32) and the Complete formula (36) is held - in either order. The lab table follow-the-formula action needs it."
37,"Game clock past 30","Early-game timer flag: game code turns it ON once the game clock passes 30 (the clock advances about 30 per room change). The room5 wrench stays hidden until then."
38,"Room4 closet unlocked","Set by using Uncle's key (13) on the room4 closet door (the key is CONSUMED - tg x, no other use). Shows the door-open animation placement (anim 3); clicking OR looking at the open door then goes inside (openclos)."
39,"Room4 closet door played","Play-once marker: the engine sets it after the door-open animation first plays. From then on the placement just shows the final open frame - the door stays open for the rest of the game."
40,"Room4 window opened","Set by opening the window in room4."
41,"Fuse fixed","Set by placing the copper penny (12) in the broken fuse (fuse-box close-up). Reveals the passage behind the room7 fireplace."
42,"Uncle cutscene done","Set by game code at the end of the room3 door cutscene (dooseq - the walk-in that reveals your dead uncle). Stops the cutscene replaying and lets you search the body."
43,"Curtains on fire","Set by lighting the room3 curtains with the matches (1). Game code then starts a countdown (about 120 time units) to the burn sequence, arms the room4 trigger event, and picks the ending variant."
44,"Saw the boat","Set by looking at the boat in the window close-up."
45,"Safe dial solved","Set by game code in the safe-dial mini-game when all three tumblers hit the combination. The safe handle needs it to open."
46,"Clock fixed","Set by placing the clockhand (23) back on the room8 clock. The mirror push needs it."
47,"Secret door open","Set by pushing the room8 mirror after the clock is fixed (46). Unlocks the hidden walkout to room9."
48,"Room9 lock picked","Set by picking the room9 door lock with the paper clip (27)."
50,"Fireplace fire out","Set by stoking out the room7 fire with the poker (2). Game code then plays the room3 door cutscene on your next visit to room3."
51,"Desk drawer unlocked","Set by using the Small Key (5) on the desk close-up drawer. Shows the open-drawer sprite (anim 9) and the syringe (anim 10); the syringe can then be looked at and taken (29). Taking it re-draws the empty drawer over the syringe."
53,"Room8 clock slid (played)","Play-once marker for the clock move animation (anim 12): set by the engine after the mirror push (47) makes the clock shake and slide. Later visits show the clock resting at its slid position. Also the trigger for the door-open animation behind it (anim 13)."
54,"Room8 secret door opened (played)","Play-once marker for the door-open animation (anim 13): chained off the clock slide (53) - the door swings open the moment the clock settles, then holds its open frame forever."
56,"Room9 door opened (played)","Play-once marker for the room9 small-door animation (anim 22): set after the lock is picked (48) and the door swings open. Later visits show it resting open."
57,"Room8 cabinet opened (played)","Play-once marker for the cabinet-door animation (anim 25): triggered by unlocking the cabinet with the paper clip (sets 25, the book). The drawer-open sprite (anim 26) needs no marker - it is a static gated on the paper (26)."
55,"Rummaged the cell food","Set by rummaging the half-eaten food tray in the room10 cell. Shows the disturbed-food overlay (anim 18) and reveals the apple (anim 19); taking the apple (28) re-draws the food over it (cover-copy placement, same trick as the desk syringe)."
56,"Room9 small door opened (played)","Play-once marker for the room9 door-open animation (anim 22): the engine sets it after picking the padlock (48) first plays the swing. Later visits show the held open frame."
58,"Room11 toolchest opened","Set by checking the toolchest in the lab (the 'Inside the toolchest is a saw' action). Shows the open-chest sprite (anim 27) over the closed chest in the background, and gates the saw grab (20). Game code re-derives it from the saw (20) every pass, healing saves made before this flag existed."
59,"Room2 vase smashed (played)","Play-once marker for the vase-smash animation (anim 30): smashing the vase with the bar (sets 5 = the Small Key, which doubles as the vase state) plays the smash once; later visits hold the broken frame."
60,"Room2 armoire opened (played)","Play-once marker for the armoire-open animation (anim 31): unlocking it with the White Key (8, sets 7) swings the doors once; later visits hold the open frame."
61,"Room3 fire cutscene played","Play-once marker for the curtain-fire full-screen cutscene (anim 33, mode seq, FIRE01-14.PIC): set by the engine after the 14-frame sequence plays on lighting the curtains (43). The player is hidden during the play (he is drawn into the frames) and returns facing west. A room load with 43 already on marks it silently - the burnt bg swap (anim 34, FIREX.PIC) already shows the end state."
62,"Pulley (item)","Inventory item: the iron pulley lashed to the beam in the pit cell (room12, below room10). Taking it shows the NOPULLY cover (anim 43). New tile 38 on INVTIL2."
63,"Room10 grate unlocked","Set by using the Apple key (22) on the small wall grate in room10. Shows the open-grate sprite (anim 42) and enables the climb to room12. The rope (14) is required to descend and sits at state 2 (hung, out of inventory) while the player is below; climbing back up returns it (walkout st=14 + aqo reset = pickup sound on arrival)."
64,"Visited-rooms bitmask (map)","NOT a flag: ob(64) holds a 12-bit mask of rooms the player has entered (bit N-1 = roomN), set by loadroom. The m-key map screen uses it to reveal only visited rooms when the map (16) is not held. Persists in saves (slot range 1-65)."
66,"Room9 trapped (gate down)","Set by the gate-slam cutscene on the FIRST entry to room9 (engine gateseq); CLEARED again by the escape (gateopen). While on: gate static (anim 48), lever-down (49), NoArrow (47) show and the east exit (obj5 cs=66) is disabled. Save range was extended to 80 flags for this puzzle."
67,"Room9 pulley on chain","Set by using the Pulley (62, consumed to state 2) on the swinging chain. Swaps the chain loop (anim 45, cond -67) for the chain+pulley loop (anim 46) and arms the rope-through-pulley escape."
68,"Room9 gate opened (solved)","Set by using the Rope (14) on the pulley: the engine gateopen cutscene plays (rope overlay, pull, lever up, gate reverse, rope removal), clears 66, and the trap never re-arms. The rope never actually leaves the inventory."
99,"(editor anchor - never set)","NOT a real flag: placements gated on 99 never draw in the game. Used to position ENGINE-drawn cutscene sprites in the editor: room9 anims 51 (pull rope), 52 (remove rope), 53 (rope on pulley) - drag these in the Hit Areas view and the gateopen cutscene follows."
